{
  "scenes": [
    {
      "role": "hook",
      "narration": "A day on Venus is longer than its year.",
      "headline": "A day longer than a year?",
      "highlight": [
        "longer"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "surprised",
        "pose": "idle"
      },
      "from": 0,
      "durationInFrames": 99
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "Here is why. Venus spins super slowly. One full spin takes about two hundred forty-three Earth days.",
      "headline": "Venus spins super slowly",
      "highlight": [
        "slowly"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "thinking",
        "pose": "pointing"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "bigNumber",
        "value": 243,
        "unit": "days",
        "label": "for Venus to spin once",
        "icon": "planet"
      },
      "from": 99,
      "durationInFrames": 218
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "But its trip around the Sun is quicker. One full orbit takes only about two hundred twenty-five Earth days.",
      "headline": "One trip around the Sun",
      "highlight": [
        "Sun"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "happy",
        "pose": "pointing"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "orbit",
        "center": "sun",
        "satellite": "planet",
        "label": "One orbit: about 225 days"
      },
      "from": 317,
      "durationInFrames": 217
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "So on Venus, one single day lasts longer than a whole year. Your birthday would come before tomorrow!",
      "headline": "The day beats the year",
      "highlight": [
        "day"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "excited",
        "pose": "jumping"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "compare",
        "unit": "days",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Venus day",
            "value": 243,
            "icon": "clock"
          },
          {
            "label": "Venus year",
            "value": 225,
            "icon": "planet"
          }
        ]
      },
      "from": 534,
      "durationInFrames": 202
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "And it gets even weirder. Venus spins backwards compared to Earth and most other planets.",
      "headline": "It spins backwards",
      "highlight": [
        "backwards"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "surprised",
        "pose": "idle"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "spotlight",
        "icon": "planet",
        "caption": "Venus spins the opposite way to Earth"
      },
      "from": 736,
      "durationInFrames": 184
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "That means on Venus, the Sun rises in the west and slowly sets in the east.",
      "headline": "Sunrise in the west",
      "highlight": [
        "west"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "wink",
        "pose": "pointing"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "steps",
        "steps": [
          {
            "icon": "sun",
            "text": "Sun rises in the west"
          },
          {
            "icon": "clock",
            "text": "Crosses the sky slowly"
          },
          {
            "icon": "moon",
            "text": "Sets in the east"
          }
        ]
      },
      "from": 920,
      "durationInFrames": 164
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "Venus is also the hottest planet in our solar system, even though Mercury is closer to the Sun.",
      "headline": "The hottest planet",
      "highlight": [
        "hottest"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "thinking",
        "pose": "idle"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "compare",
        "unit": "°C",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Venus",
            "value": 475,
            "icon": "fire"
          },
          {
            "label": "Mercury by day",
            "value": 430,
            "icon": "sun"
          }
        ]
      },
      "from": 1084,
      "durationInFrames": 198
    },
    {
      "role": "fact",
      "narration": "Its thick clouds trap heat, so the ground reaches about four hundred seventy-five degrees Celsius. Hot enough to melt lead!",
      "headline": "Hot enough to melt lead",
      "highlight": [
        "melt lead"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "surprised",
        "pose": "jumping"
      },
      "visual": {
        "layout": "bigNumber",
        "value": 475,
        "unit": "°C",
        "label": "on the ground of Venus",
        "icon": "thermometer"
      },
      "from": 1282,
      "durationInFrames": 234
    },
    {
      "role": "recap",
      "narration": "Quick recap. Venus spins slowly and backwards, so its day is longer than its year.",
      "headline": "Quick recap",
      "highlight": [
        "recap"
      ],
      "pip": {
        "expression": "happy",
        "pose": "pointing"
      },
